  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06YU">Definition <span data-tag="06YU">21.17.13</span>.</a> Let $(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{O})$ be a ringed site. Let $\mathcal{F}^\bullet $ be an object of $D(\mathcal{O})$. The <em>derived tensor product</em> </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  - \otimes _\mathcal {O}^{\mathbf{L}} \mathcal{F}^\bullet : D(\mathcal{O}) \longrightarrow D(\mathcal{O})  \]
</div>
  <p> is the exact functor of triangulated categories described above. </p>
